==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[rite]] [[of]] [[passage]]|rites of passage}}

# {{context|anthropology|lang=en}} a ceremony or series of ceremonies, often very ritualized, to celebrate a transition in a person’s life. [[baptism|Baptisms]], [[bar mitzvah]]s, [[wedding]]s and [[funeral]]s are among the best known examples.
#: ''After John officially attained his majority, Robert bought him his first legal beer. This is a common American '''rite of passage'''.''

